error[SC0411]: `*b` is read before anything was assigned to it
   ╭─[ a_block_no_call_may_reach_is_still_read_unwritten_for_certain_after_a_call.c:7:12 ]
   │
 7 │     return *b != 0;
   │            ───┬───  
   │               ╰───── read here
───╯
  = note: C17 7.22.3.1 p2 and 7.22.3.4 p2 leave what `aligned_alloc` and `malloc` allocate indeterminate until something writes it, and Annex J.2 lists using that value as undefined
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = help: assign to it before reading it, or allocate with `calloc`
